{"type": "tool_call", "n": 14, "ts": 1790154279.860933, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "DE March 2026 Cutoff & Journal-Entry Review \u2014 Summary\n\nScope: Reviewed all 28 DE ledger entries posted in period 2026-03 for cutoff accuracy and support.\n\nFindings & Actions:\n\n1. CUTOFF ERROR CORRECTED \u2014 JE-00305 (Nordwolke Hosting, \"NW-2026-0402 - dedicated cluster\", EUR 5,600.00)\n   - Booked 2026-03-31 to account 5000/2000, but underlying vendor bill (DOC-0206) is dated 2026-04-02 and explicitly states \"Leistungszeitraum / Service period: April 2026 (2026-04-01 to 2026-04-30).\"\n   - This was a March/April cutoff error \u2014 the cost belongs entirely to April.\n   - Reversed via JE-00306 (dated 2026-03-31, supported by DOC-0206), removing the EUR 5,600 expense/AP from March.\n   - Attempted to re-book the correct entry into April 2026 but the system reports only period 2026-03 is currently open for posting. The re-booking (Dr 5000 / Cr 2000, EUR 5,600, supported by DOC-0206) must be posted once the April period opens \u2014 flagging this for the team/controller so it isn't missed at April open.\n\n2. UNSUPPORTED ENTRY \u2014 FLAGGED AS EXCEPTION (EXC-001) \u2014 JE-00298 (\"Umsatzkorrektur Q1\", EUR 9,999.00, dated 2026-03-29)\n   - Manual entry (Dr AR 1100 / Cr Revenue 4000) posted by m.krause at 23:47, no supporting document attached.\n   - Searched invoices, credit memos, schedules and correspondence for backup \u2014 found none. Cannot identify the customer, the basis for the \"Q1 revenue correction,\" or confirm it belongs in March.\n   - Logged as exception EXC-001 for controller follow-up with m.krause; recommend reversal if support cannot be produced before lock.\n\n3. All other 26 DE entries in March (subscription invoices, AP bills/payments, card transactions, payroll and payroll funding transfers) were reviewed against invoice/receipt dates and service periods, all have support attached, and all were posted in the correct period consistent with prior-month patterns (e.g., JE-00234 Nordwolke NOR-92853 billed and booked in March for March service, same pattern as Feb's NOR-34031). No further cutoff issues identified.\n\nNet impact of corrections: March 2026 DE hosting expense (account 5000) reduced by EUR 5,600 (cutoff correction); EUR 9,999 of AR/Revenue remains under exception review pending controller resolution \u2014 period should not be locked until EXC-001 is resolved.\n\nOutstanding action items for controller/team before lock:\n- Resolve EXC-001 (JE-00298) \u2014 obtain support or reverse.\n- Once April 2026 period opens, post the Nordwolke Hosting April cluster charge (Dr 5000 / Cr 2000, EUR 5,600, support DOC-0206) that could not be posted today due to period lock."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 6}
